RayCAD patch to OCCT 8.0.1 (LGPL-2.1 with the OCCT exception; this file is under the same terms).

What: ChFi3d_Builder::Compute, where it raises vertex tolerances to those of the new curves ("Update tolerances on
vertex to max adjacent edges"), skips a curve point interference whose geometry index does not name a vertex of the
data structure, instead of reading that shape as a vertex.

Why: for some fillets the interference is of kind TopOpeBRepDS_VERTEX but myDS->Shape(gi) is not a vertex.
TopoDS::Vertex does not check the type in a release build (No_Exception), so BRep_Tool::Tolerance reads past the end
of the smaller TShape and BRep_Builder::UpdateVertex then writes there: valgrind reports "Invalid read of size 8"
(BRep_Tool::Tolerance) and "Invalid write of size 8" (BRep_Builder::UpdateVertex) from ChFi3d_Builder::Compute,
24 bytes after a 64-byte block. The corrupted heap crashed later, at random places (a ChFi3d_Builder destructor,
BSplSLib_Cache evaluation in BRepLib::SameParameter) or aborted in malloc, in about half the runs of RayCAD's naming
holdout block 6 (sequence 18:0, a fillet, BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet), on Linux and Windows, single-threaded too.
Skipping the interference only leaves that shape's tolerance as it is.

Upstream: not reported.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder.cxx
@@ -428,6 +428,13 @@
           }
           TopOpeBRepDS_Kind gk = II->GeometryType();
           int               gi = II->Geometry();
+          // RayCAD: the geometry of a vertex interference must be a vertex of the DS. Another shape read as a
+          // vertex is read, and its tolerance written, past the end of its TShape (heap corruption).
+          if (gk == TopOpeBRepDS_VERTEX
+              && (myDS->Shape(gi).IsNull() || myDS->Shape(gi).ShapeType() != TopAbs_VERTEX))
+          {
+            continue;
+          }
           if (gk == TopOpeBRepDS_VERTEX)
           {
             const TopoDS_Vertex& v    = TopoDS::Vertex(myDS->Shape(gi));
